 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>“2. There is no security in the system [under the proposed new U.S. Constitution], either for the rights of [people with different ideas] or the liberty of the Press. . . .</p>\n<p>4. The Executive and the Legislative are so dangerously [combined] . . . that [it should cause people to be alarmed]. . . .</p>\n<p>9. There is no [system] for [making sure that power does not stay] in the same hands for life.”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">This excerpt is from “Observations on the New Constitution and on the Federal and State Conventions,” by Mercy Otis Warren. It originally appeared as a newspaper article in the spring of 1788.</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided.</i></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 615006,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which of the following groups would agree with Warren’s excerpt?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167996,
     "content_html": "Patriots"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167995,
     "content_html": "Loyalists"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167994,
     "content_html": "Federalists"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167997,
     "content_html": "Anti-Federalists"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 615007,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The sentiments expressed in the excerpt provided contributed to which of the following events?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1168000,
     "content_html": "Jail time for Warren for being a woman in open defiance of the majority opinion"
    },
    {
     "id": 1168001,
     "content_html": "Public demands that a bill of rights be added to the Constitution to address some of these concerns"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167999,
     "content_html": "A third convention that once again debated a new form of government agreeable to all citizens"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167998,
     "content_html": "The end of Warren’s ability to publicly publish her writings"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 615008,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What outside information would a historian use to contextualize the sentiment in this document?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1168004,
     "content_html": "Warren’s attack on the Adams family, which ruined their friendship and prevented reconciliation"
    },
    {
     "id": 1168005,
     "content_html": "Warren’s strict adherence to Revolutionary values of liberty and self-government"
    },
    {
     "id": 1168003,
     "content_html": "Warren’s viewpoint as a woman, which gave her insight her male peers missed"
    },
    {
     "id": 1168002,
     "content_html": "Warren’s provocative nature, which meant she wrote incendiary notes intentionally"
    }
   ],
